{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/769092-brainstorming-a-new-daeva-bloodline","id":769092,"title":"Brainstorming a New Daeva Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T04:13:17-08:00","id":769092,"title":"Brainstorming a New Daeva Bloodline","content":"Hey there, just writing for some help in developing a new bloodline for clan Daeva--one based on such older vampire figures as Lord Ruthven and Varney.<br /> <br /> I call them the <i>Achelois</i>, I call them the <i>Achelois</i>, named after the minor Greek lunar deity hailed for her healing powers (her very name meaning &quot;she who washes away pain&quot;). They are a Daeva bloodline, famous for their taste for the blood of the &quot;innocent&quot; or young maidens, and having their vitality tied to the moon and its phases...<br /> <br /> In a word, although their bodies will slowly repair themselves like other vampires in the daysleep, they are completely unable to spend blood points in order to regenerate their wounds. Instead, the touch of direct moonlight is what they use to heal their bodies. They are known to be nigh-unstoppable under the light of the full moon, but being exceptionally vulnerable on moonless nights...and are famous for their strange hunger for the blood of the innocent.<br /> <br /> That's what I'm starting out with...like the idea thus far? What other things would you like to see in this bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 11-22-2015, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T04:56:16-08:00","id":769115,"title":"","content":"I'll probably give them Dominate as a fourth discipline, given the powers exibited by Lord Ruthven. The Moon ties could be both their Bloodline weakness and their Bloodline Boon. The weakness will imply being unable to control their healing just by pumping blood like any other kindred. For the boon I picture the different phases of the moon (new, crescent, middle, gibous and full) working as the number of health levels healed, say 0-4 Bashing per turn <i>or</i> half that in Lethal. Aggravated damage will only be able to be healed under the full moon, maybe a level per night?<br /> <br /> EDIT: of course the healing only works as long as the moonlight shines on them, so while under roof they will be as screwed as in the nights of new moon, when they cannot heal <i>at all.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-19-2015, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:56:57-08:00","id":769198,"title":"","content":"I think the healing aspect is a change too big from the standard rules.may be an option could be that in full moon they can triple the standard healing, while in new moon, their healing habilities are one third of the normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:40:31-08:00","id":769435,"title":"","content":"Or, the Vitae/turn varies but only in regard to healing. Say at Half Moon is as per the standard Blood Potency, at Gibous at BP+1 and at Full Moon BP+2, on the other hand at Crescent is BP-1 and at New Moon BP-2, if that would put Vitae per turn at 0 or under, they just cannot heal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:37:39-08:00","id":770208,"title":"","content":"Interesting responses....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/769092-brainstorming-a-new-daeva-bloodline?p=769198#post769198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the healing aspect is a change too big from the standard rules</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you really think so?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:51:18-08:00","id":771510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/769092-brainstorming-a-new-daeva-bloodline?p=769115#post769115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Moon ties could be both their Bloodline weakness and their Bloodline Boon. The weakness will imply being unable to control their healing just by pumping blood like any other kindred. For the boon I picture the different phases of the moon (new, crescent, middle, gibous and full) working as the number of health levels healed, say 0-4 Bashing per turn <i>or</i> half that in Lethal. Aggravated damage will only be able to be healed under the full moon, maybe a level per night?<br /> <br /> EDIT: of course the healing only works as long as the moonlight shines on them, so while under roof they will be as screwed as in the nights of new moon, when they cannot heal <i>at all.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a great application for it, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T09:37:25-08:00","id":771540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/769092-brainstorming-a-new-daeva-bloodline?p=770208#post770208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really think so?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not just from a combat standpoint, but a social one as well. Vampires are figuratively sharks. You bleed, you walk into elysium reeking of blood? Imagine the harpies mocking you, calling you out for being griviously hurt by a wind? None of these are a good thing. That's a very hefty drawback there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:21:12-08:00","id":771617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/769092-brainstorming-a-new-daeva-bloodline?p=771540#post771540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not just from a combat standpoint, but a social one as well. Vampires are figuratively sharks. You bleed, you walk into elysium reeking of blood? Imagine the harpies mocking you, calling you out for being griviously hurt by a wind? None of these are a good thing. That's a very hefty drawback there.</div> </div> </div> </div>well more like the drawback is actually that if you're hurt you just don't show up at Elysium because you are a walking Masquerade breach and the Invictus is going to ask for your head if you are out in public looking and smelling like that, but that's hardly the harshest bloodline weakness ever. I mean, there are Nosferatu that have to stay in complete darkness or they basically start hallucinating...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:54:16-08:00","id":771629,"title":"","content":"However, Nosferatu can get around with their natural affinity for Obfuscate. They're meant to be the creepy ones in the shadows. Daeva? They're designed to be in the spotlight. Its part of their nature, and the theme of the clan. That's a major difference. One aids in play, the other has the potential to destroy you utterly or even remove you from play. That's a bad weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T06:39:31-08:00","id":772263,"title":"","content":"Sorry, my post wasn't very clear. I was referring to the Lygos bloodline (Nosferatu clanbook). If there's any light at all they get distracted by creepy hallucinations and a sense of horrible wrongness. Now <i>this </i>is a harsh weakness.<br /> <br /> Anyway I'm all for a weakness that merely makes healing difficult and costly, and not entirely impossible, as that would be very crippling just like you said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}